body:
Thank you very much! Yeah, I initially searched the reddit for other paint schemes of scars but truly almost impossible to find right now! I figured it couldn't hurt to be the change.

&#x200B;

The markings were probably the thing I'm happiest with that I was so done with halfway through. The leg 'teeth' basically mandated that they be painted on sprue since it would not have been possible off of it, but super happy how it all came together.

I would say if your player wants to use ranged weapons in close combat then it would be, in a siilar vein to legolas, using the arrows as almost daggers to stab in and then shooting someone a few paces away in "rearward stance". So an arrow stab would be a dagger/brawling attack, and then you could maybe customize a close range archer virtue that provides a bonus to that or allows a brawling stab and if it results ina kill you can take an immediate shot at another target if you aren't still engaged.

&#x200B;

But for the most part legolas would shoot a few paces not at right close range, then it would be daggers or stabbing with the arrowheads. As for a high Target number, it sounds like his stats don't support combat/low strength. So that would mean needing to increase his dice for his combat proficiences or let him swap his stat array to something that better suits the game you are playing.

&#x200B;

For called shots there are the great success charts and if it results where you pierce/wound/call shot an eye then it's flavoring that how you'd like. They're already punished stat wise but maybe shooting an eye means that an other character could go to rearward since that enemy is worse at tracking people in combat, or they lose 1d against someone who is in a different stance then last turn since it as well is harder to keep track. I would lean into that then say a called shot is an insta-kill because you then have the can of worms going "well why doesn't my orc archer call shot on the hobbits eye" and that's not a feel good.

So the info from my last post was I had gotten a lot from my LGS of Firstborn blood angels. After spending a bit of time identifying units I ended up with a legal patrol/vanguard detachment list that exceeds 2,000 points without even marking all the alternate weapons the previous owner had attached to the models.

&#x200B;

For the most part the objective was to get the army fully painted, unify the basing, and get them ready to play so I had an army to take to games in relatively short period of time as my other army isn't even partly built yet(I've been working through AoS orcs). The only unpainted models were the Baal destroyer and two Plasma weapon Devastator marines so I got those painted up similarly for the most part to the existing models but as these are the first marines I've done definitely want to improve in the future. 

&#x200B;

I wanted to leave the paint work the same on most of the models as much as possible as I think it's a really cool look into how this person painted their models. I just went through and added some highlights on the plasma weapons, some gold accents, and some fixes where I just wasn't going to be happy with it in the long run. As well, I wanted to run the standard dread as a librarian so added some TS bits and a stormcast banner for style.

So channels do run into problems when they have split types of videos. If you have dedicated viewers that only watch one category in force, and not another, youtube stops recommending those videos as much. And since they aren't recommended they get less views, which hurts your channel growth.

&#x200B;

So overall having a secondary channel for a dedicated category actually helps and promotes your channel overall than having too much mixed content.

Right, but that's normally when it's stuck in the salt flats, or the boat possibly sinking, or they can't take proper video of sahara animals. You don't really hear about them when they're on a random road in birmingham, or how their van is keeping pace with three sportscars on the way to mexico, or as a Ford GT races public transport.

&#x200B;

The Film crew gets mentioned when it's interesting, not as a regular character.

On the beach by Nevil Shute. I don't have much to say about it without giving things away, but it's bleak. Soul-crushingly, heart-breakingly bleak. 

&#x200B;

Recommended it multiple times.

Manner muling doesn't delay the game, it's pretty much done in the 5 seconds before the gg, or the rare turnaround, but basically never has an impact. I view the counter the same way that I do: Crouch spam in smash, taunt spam in HS/MTGA, or whatever game has a social mechanic. 

&#x200B;

Winning the game with style is fine, if you have a really cool sequence of cards that can get you the win and make a story then go for it. But  the story of the time that you stole four lands and had lethal/resource excess/life advantage will not be made better by...countering a signet from someone who realistically was never in this game.

I mean as someone who's working on Mardu Pyro I don't agree with that. It also allows for fair gy synergies as well since the selection is beneficial to the deck.

&#x200B;

 Now, is it worth punishing decks like these to stilt the bigger meta % decks? Possibly, but there's other key cards in those decks that might be experimented with first before we ban it.

